1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,450
Why We Celebrate New Year.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:06,775
New Year celebrations are among humanity's oldest traditions.

3
00:00:06,775 --> 00:00:12,725
Babylonians celebrated the new year 4,000 years ago with an 11-day religious festival.

4
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:21,487
Julius Caesar established January 1 as the Roman New Year, naming the month after Janus, the two-faced god looking backward and forward.

5
00:00:21,487 --> 00:00:33,487
Different cultures observe different dates: Chinese New Year falls between late January and February; Rosh Hashanah occurs in September or October; the Islamic New Year shifts through the solar year.

6
00:00:33,487 --> 00:00:41,375
Common themes unite these diverse traditions: reflection on the past, resolutions to improve, and gathering with family.

7
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:46,800
The transition between years universally prompts both reflection and hope for renewal.

